  "name": "Question 3",
  "problem": "Calculate the minor of the entry ${p}_{31}$ in the matrix\n$P=[\\begin{aligned}-11 & 7 & -9 \\\\ 2 & -2 & 9 \\\\ 8 & -5 & 72\\end{aligned}].$",
  "worked_solution": "The minor of ${p}_{31}=8$ (third row, first column) is the determinant of the remaining entries when the column and row containing $8$ are removed: \n\n$$\nP=[\\begin{aligned}\u2217 & 7 & -9 \\\\ \u2217 & -2 & 9 \\\\ 8 & \u2217 & \u2217\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nSo, the minor of ${p}_{31}=8$ is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{det}[\\begin{aligned}7 & -9 \\\\ -2 & 9\\end{aligned}] & =|\\begin{aligned}7 & -9 \\\\ -2 & 9\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =7\\cdot 9-(-9)\\cdot (-2) \\\\  & =63-18 \\\\  & =45.\\end{aligned}\n$$",
